# OpenCS Labs -- notebook image, top-level requirements.
#
# This is the human-edited input file. It intentionally uses loose lower bounds
# only: the reproducible, fully pinned set that the image actually installs is
# `requirements.lock` (compile this file, then pin every resolved version).
#
# Every package here is part of the course contract in HLD.md section 11: a
# student notebook that works on one deployment must work on every deployment,
# so all of these must exist in the image and are exercised by
# `smoke-tests/test_environment.py`.
#
# Regenerating the lock:
#   python -m piptools compile --generate-hashes=false requirements.in \
#       --output-file requirements.lock   # then re-add the header block
#
# --- Jupyter stack ---------------------------------------------------------
jupyterlab>=4.4,<5
# Provides jupyterhub-singleuser: the Hub authenticates the single-user server's
# API token, so this must live in the notebook image, not only in the Hub image.
